HST Office: UX fixes found in the beta.3 usability review.

- Help > License Information: the summary under the source-code notice is a fixed
  Vietnamese text in every UI language. It carries the HST copyright line
  ("© 2026 HASON TECH · © 2000–2026 The Document Foundation và các tác giả LibreOffice"),
  keeps the MPL-2.0, third-party and OpenOffice.org attributions, and drops the upstream
  "All rights reserved" line and the upstream website URL.
- Tools > Options > Load/Save > HTML Compatibility: the Basic export checkbox reads
  "%PRODUCTNAME Basic" (it said "LibreOffice Basic" in the English UI; the Vietnamese
  translation already used %PRODUCTNAME).
- Extension Manager > Add: in UI languages other than Vietnamese the install confirmation shows
  the HST third-party notice in English (the generic upstream text had no notice; the
  Vietnamese translation already carries it).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/cui/uiconfig/ui/opthtmlpage.ui
+++ b/cui/uiconfig/ui/opthtmlpage.ui
@@ -626,7 +626,7 @@
                 </child>
                 <child>
                   <object class="GtkCheckButton" id="starbasic">
-                    <property name="label" translatable="yes" context="opthtmlpage|starbasic">LibreOffice _Basic</property>
+                    <property name="label" translatable="yes" context="opthtmlpage|starbasic">%PRODUCTNAME _Basic</property>
                     <property name="visible">True</property>
                     <property name="can-focus">True</property>
                     <property name="receives-default">False</property>
